{"segs": ["PA_ja_85:0.2"], "en": "Ekakanipāta,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_85:0.3"], "en": "Apāyimhavagga", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_85:0.4"], "en": "5. The Kimpakka Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_85:1.1", "PA_ja_85:1.2"], "en": "“He who indulges in sensual pleasures without knowing that they will lead to future harm;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_85:1.3"], "en": "\"At the end of its ripening, it destroys him,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_85:1.4"], "en": "like eating the *kiṃpāka* fruit.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_85:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the fifth Jātaka, the *Kiṃpāka-jātaka*.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
